# doomcode key bindings: ~/.config/doomcode/keys
#
# Every line below is a built-in default, so this file changes nothing
# until you edit it. Each line is "key action"; "prefix key action" binds
# the key after Ctrl-B; "key -" removes a binding; "key run command" runs
# a command like button 2; "key tag text" types text into the tag.
# Keys: C-x (Ctrl), Cmd-x, M-x (Alt/Option), S- (Shift) with special keys
# such as C-S-Left; Left Right Up Down Home End PgUp PgDn Ins Del
# Backspace Tab Enter Esc Space F1-F12; C-/ is Ctrl+/.
# "Keys actions" lists every action; after a change: Keys reload.
#
# You only need the lines you change; delete the rest if you like.

0xF800       cursor-down
C-/          comment-toggle
C-Backspace  delete-word-back
C-Del        delete-word-forward
C-Down       scroll-down
C-End        file-end
C-Enter      execute
C-Home       file-start
C-Left       word-left
C-Right      word-right
C-S-Left     select-word-left
C-S-Right    select-word-right
C-Up         scroll-up
C-a          select-all
C-c          snarf
C-d          select-word
C-e          execute
C-f          find
C-g          goto
C-k          kill-line
C-l          select-line
C-n          new
C-o          look
C-s          put
C-v          paste
C-x          cut
C-y          redo
C-z          undo
